P18-V01 Remoting close-socket system-property source follow-up (`280bcfe0`,
2026-10-16): the invoked Java `ClientConfigPropertiesProbe` now sets
`com.rocketmq.remoting.client.closeSocketIfTimeout=false` and records
`NettyClientConfig.isClientCloseSocketIfTimeout()` in
`fixtures/runtime/client-config-properties.json`. Java source uses
`Boolean.parseBoolean`, which recognizes case-insensitive `true` without
trimming. Rust reads the same key from process environment on the first
`ClientConfig::default()`, applies equivalent parsing, and retains the value in
the same process-wide `OnceLock` as the two semaphore defaults. The isolated
`client_remoting_defaults_follow_java_system_properties` test checks the Java
fixture values and malformed semaphore integer rejection.

